  "title": "Me llamo Ana",
  "titleEn": "My name is Ana",
  "blurbEn": "Your first text. Meet Ana, learn to say who you are and where you live, and see how Spanish gives every noun a gender.",
  "grammarRefs": ["ser-basics", "gender-and-articles"],
  "body": "Hola. Me llamo Ana y soy de España. Vivo en Madrid.\n\nMadrid es una ciudad grande. Mi casa es pequeña, pero es bonita.\n\nTengo un gato. Se llama Michi. Es un gato negro y muy simpático.\n\n¿Y tú? ¿Cómo te llamas? ¿De dónde eres?",
  "translationEn": "Hello. My name is Ana and I am from Spain. I live in Madrid.\n\nMadrid is a big city. My house is small, but it is pretty.\n\nI have a cat. His name is Michi. He is a black cat and very friendly.\n\nAnd you? What is your name? Where are you from?",
